      "title": "Use the Python UTF-8 mode for `asn2wrs.py`",
      "message": "Use the Python UTF-8 mode for `asn2wrs.py`\n\nSome of the input files to this script contain non-ASCII characters, encoded\nwith UTF-8. On Windows, the default encoding is usually not UTF-8, so reading\nfiles opened without an explicit `encoding` argument can result in\n`UnicodeDecodeError` exceptions. Enabling the UTF-8 mode makes UTF-8 the default\nencoding regardless of the system encoding, preventing this problem.\n\nThe UTF-8 mode was added in Python 3.7. To keep compatibility with Python 3.6,\nenable it via the `PYTHONUTF8` environment variable (rather than the `-X utf8`\noption), since the variable will just be ignored by versions of Python\nthat don't support it.\n",
      "author_name": "Roman Donchenko",
